&lt;p style="font: 11pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Regulatory assets are pension benefit obligations
which will be recovered in future rates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The COVID-19 related amount is the late fees
and associated costs the Company was not allowed to charge customers during the pandemic. The Public Service Commission of Wisconsin directed
the Company to amortize these costs over five years effective June 18, 2025.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 11pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 3 &#xFFFD;
DEFERRED CHARGES &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;(Continued)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The storm damage repair costs are costs incurred
to restore power to customers due to damage from a significant ice and snow storm which occurred in December of 2022. The Public Service
Commission of Wisconsin directed the Company to amortize these costs over five years effective June 18, 2025.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/97% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The defined pension plan additional contribution
is an additional funding contribution the Company was required to make to the plan. The Company offers eligible employees the option of
taking their pension payout in the form of an annuity or a lump sum payment. The Company has been notified by its actuarial firm that
in order to provide the lump sum benefit option available within the plan to all of its employees, regardless of annual income, the plan
must be funded at 110 percent of the Internal Revenue Service defined pension liability. On April 13, 2022, the Company&#xFFFD;s request
filed with the Public Service Commission of Wisconsin was approved to defer the additional 2022 contribution to its pension plan. The
Company is waiting for direction from the Public Service Commission of Wisconsin to determine a plan to recapture these incurred costs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/90% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt/90% Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

