&lt;p style="font: 11pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 11pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 8 &#xFFFD; DEFERRED
TAXES &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;(Continued)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Corporate taxes are paid on customer contributions
in aid to construction in the year the contributions are received. These taxes are then amortized against current operations over the
average life of the affected plant accounts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Accrued vacation and sick pay are also recorded to
recognize the tax attributes of accrued employee benefit liabilities recognized on the financial statements but not deducted for tax purposes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Allowance for credit losses is recorded to recognize
the tax attributes of allowing for uncollectable accounts recognized on the financial statements but not deducted for tax purposes until
account is written off.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Depreciation adjustments between tax methods and
book methods result in income tax effects. These adjustments are being amortized over the lives of each plant account.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;On December 22, 2017 the Tax Cuts and Job Act (TCJA)
was signed into law. One major provision of this new law was the reduction of federal corporate income taxes to a flat rate of 21%. The
Company had previously been subject to a 34% corporate federal tax rate. These deferred income taxes had previously been recorded based
upon a 34% federal corporate income tax rate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Therefore, at January 1, 2018, the Company calculated
the change in deferred corporate taxes from the 34% rate to the new 21% rate. These changes are summarized below:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif"&gt;
  &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: bottom"&gt;
    &lt;td style="width: 66%"&gt;Accrued vacation and sick pay&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right; width: 16%"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right; width: 2%"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right; width: 16%"&gt;$&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;13,307&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr style="vertical-align: bottom"&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;Contributions in aid of construction&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;261,470&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: left"&gt;Property, plant and equipment depreciation&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: bottom; text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: bottom; text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: bottom; border-bottom: Black 0.5pt solid; text-align: right"&gt;(657,593)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr style="vertical-align: bottom"&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr style="vertical-align: bottom"&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold"&gt;TOTAL REDUCTION&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; border-bottom: Black 2pt double; text-align: right"&gt;$&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;(382,816)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;


&lt;p style="font: 11pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The Company has, under Public Service Commission
guidance, begun amortization of these amounts. The accrued vacation and sick pay portion of the tax reduction was recorded in its entirety
during 2018; the contributions in aid of construction and depreciation portions will be amortized over an annual schedule which runs through
2050. Amortization in &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2025&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2024&lt;/font&gt;
totaled $20,024 and $20,315 in credits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 14pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 9 &#xFFFD; INCOME TAXES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 7pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;Income tax provisions for the years ended December
31 are as follows:&lt;/p&gt;

