&lt;p style="font: 11pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 11pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;The Company has taken
no uncertain tax positions which it believes would require special disclosure.&lt;br style="clear: both" /&gt;
&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 10 &#xFFFD; OPERATING RATIOS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;On June 18, 2025 the Public Service Commission of
Wisconsin authorized the company to increase rates on average of 4.04%, authorizing 8.65% return on average investment in net utility
plant and materials inventory and 10.75% return on average stockholders&#xFFFD; equity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;As of December 31 the ratios were as follows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif"&gt;
  &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle; width: 70%"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle; border-bottom: Black 0.5pt solid; text-align: right; width: 14%"&gt;2025&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; width: 2%"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle; border-bottom: Black 0.5pt solid; text-align: right; width: 14%"&gt;2024&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle"&gt;Return on average investment in net utility plant and materials&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: right"&gt;7.18%&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: right"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: right"&gt;6.28%&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: left"&gt;Return on average stockholders&#xFFFD; equity&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: right"&gt;6.68%&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td style="vertical-align: middle; text-align: right"&gt;5.62%&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;


&lt;p style="font: 11pt Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 14pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 11 &#xFFFD; DEFINED CONTRIBUTION PLAN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The Company also maintains a defined contribution
401(k) pension plan. Employee contributions to this plan are partially matched by company contributions. The Company match is 40% for
every dollar contributed, up to 6% of income for a maximum Company exposure of 2.4% of eligible employee payroll. This plan is available
to all full time Company employees. In &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2025&lt;/font&gt;, an employee could contribute
up to the IRS maximum which was $23,500 to $31,000, depending on the employee&#xFFFD;s age. Contributions are deposited with an outside
plan trustee, who is responsible for all investing, payment of proceeds, and reporting. Contributions to the 401(k) plan by the Company
for &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2025&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2024&lt;/font&gt;
were $30,526 and $27,255.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 14pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 12 &#xFFFD; COMMITMENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The Company is committed to purchase its electric
power and energy with various vendors through June 30, 2036.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 14pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE 13 &#xFFFD; MAJOR SUPPLIER INFORMATION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The Company purchased approximately 75% and 55% of
its electric power from AEP Energy Partners, Inc. for the year ended &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;December
31, 2025&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2024&lt;/font&gt;, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The Company purchased approximately 21% and 33% of
its electric power from Renewable World Energies, LLC for the year ended &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;December
31, 2025&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font style="font-weight: normal; text-transform: none"&gt;2024&lt;/font&gt;, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font: 12pt Calibri, Helvetica, Sans-Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"&gt;The Company purchased approximately 4% and 11% of
